[219.049866, "i", "cat > /home/user/BUGFIX_SUMMARY.txt << 'EOF'\n=================================================================\nDISTRIBUTED TF-IDF PIPELINE - BUG FIX SUMMARY\n=================================================================\n\nPROBLEM:\n--------\nThe distributed feature extraction pipeline was producing incorrect output:\n- Only 12k/50k rows in output (massive data loss)\n- TF-IDF scores > 1 (mathematically impossible)\n- No errors or crashes (silent data corruption)\n\nROOT CAUSES IDENTIFIED:\n-----------------------\n\n1. INDEPENDENT VOCABULARIES PER CHUNK (Critical Bug)\n   - Each worker created its own TfidfVectorizer\n   - Workers called fit_transform() on individual chunks\n   - This created different vocabularies for each chunk\n   - When coordinator concatenated results, columns didn't align\n   - Result: Data corruption, invalid scores, wrong feature counts\n\n2. RACE CONDITION (Data Loss)\n   - Coordinator sent chunks immediately after binding sockets\n   - Workers hadn't connected yet when chunks were sent\n   - Early ch"]
[219.049998, "i", "unks were dropped by ZeroMQ\n   - Result: Missing data, only ~12k/50k rows processed\n\n3. NO CHUNK TRACKING (Potential Duplicates)\n   - Coordinator used a list to collect results\n   - No deduplication or verification of chunk IDs\n   - Could process duplicates or miss chunks silently\n\n4. TIMEOUT-BASED COLLECTION (Unreliable)\n   - 5-second timeout for receiving results\n   - Could exit before all workers finished\n   - No guarantee all chunks were processed\n\nFIXES APPLIED:\n--------------\n\n1. SHARED VOCABULARY (coordinator.py)\n   - Fit TfidfVectorizer on FULL dataset before chunking\n   - Send fitted vectorizer to all workers first\n   - Workers use transform() only, not fit_transform()\n   - Ensures consistent feature columns across all chunks\n\n2. PROPER SYNCHRONIZATION (coordinator.py)\n   - Added 2-second delay for workers to connect\n   - Send vectorizer first, wait, then send chunks\n   - Eliminates race condition and data loss\n\n3. CHUNK TRACKING (coordinator.py)\n   - Use dict instead of list to track results by chun"]
[219.050045, "i", "k_id\n   - Detect and ignore duplicate results\n   - Wait for exact number of chunks (50/50)\n   - Aggregate results in correct order\n\n4. WORKER PROTOCOL (worker.py)\n   - Receive and store fitted vectorizer first\n   - Use vectorizer.transform() on chunks\n   - Handle message types (VECTORIZER vs CHUNK)\n   - Ensure all workers use same vocabulary\n\nRESULTS:\n--------\nAfter fixes:\n✓ All 50,000 rows processed correctly\n✓ TF-IDF values in valid range [0.0, 0.7998]\n✓ 100 features (as specified by max_features=100)\n✓ No data loss, no duplicates, no corruption\n✓ Consistent with single-threaded reference implementation\n\nKEY LESSON:\n-----------\nIn distributed TF-IDF, the vocabulary MUST be fitted on the complete\ndataset, then shared across all workers. Each worker should only\ntransform its chunks using the shared vocabulary. Fitting independently\nper chunk creates incompatible feature spaces that cannot be merged.\n\n=================================================================\nEOF\n"]
[219.050071, "o", "cat > /home/user/BUGFIX_SUMMARY.txt << 'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rk_id\r\n   - Detect and ignore duplicate results\r\n   - W"]
[219.0501, "o", "ait for exact number of chunks (50/50)\r\n   - Aggregate results in correct order\r\n\r\n4. WORKER PROTOCOL (wor"]
[219.050135, "o", "ker.py)\r\n   - Receive and store fitted vectorizer first\r\n   - Use vectorizer.transform() on chunks\r\n   - Handle message types (VECTORIZER vs"]
[219.050165, "o", " CHUNK)\r\n   - Ensure all workers use same vocabulary\r\n\r\nRESULTS:\r\n--------\r\nAfter fixes:\r\n✓ All 50,000 rows process"]
[219.050194, "o", "ed correctly\r\n✓ TF-IDF values in valid range [0.0, 0.7998]\r\n✓ 100 feature"]
[219.050219, "o", "s (as specified by max_featur"]
[219.050245, "o", "es=100)\r\n✓ No data loss, no duplicates, no corruption\r\n✓ Consistent with "]
[219.050271, "o", "single-threaded reference implementation\r\n\r\nKEY LESSON:\r\n-----------\r\nIn distributed TF-IDF, the vocabula"]
[219.050296, "o", "ry MUST be fitted on the complete\r\ndataset, then shared across all workers. Each worker should only\r\ntransform its chunks u"]
[219.050326, "o", "sing the shared vocabulary. Fitting independently\r\nper chunk creates incompatible "]
[219.050357, "o", "feature spaces that cannot be merged.\r\n\r\n=================================================================\r\nEOF\r\n"]
